{
  "format": "bgsim.subsystem",
  "name": "RevoluteLink3D",
  "description": "One link of a spatial serial chain: the offset T from the parent body's frame to the joint, the compliant joint J (Revolute3D), the offset Link from the joint's child frame to the body's centre of mass, the body B (RigidBody3D) on its 1-junction BJ, and the pose band W = gp o LN o J.pose, P = W o LC that B's gravity reads. Ports: parent (bond in, from the parent body's junction or the ground), child (the body junction, bond out to the next link's parent), drive (the joint's Rotation drive port), gp (the parent joint's child-frame pose in), g (this joint's child-frame pose out), q and qd (joint angle and rate), V and gb (the body twist and the body pose). Every offset, the joint parameters, the body and the joint's start values are pinned. Generated by design/serial_link.py.",
